# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# User data now lives in the data root, outside this repo (src/config.py,
# backlog/share-as-toolkit-plan.md §3.1). These paths are ignored so that a
# not-yet-migrated checkout, or a data root that happens to sit inside the repo,
# can never commit someone's job search.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEADING slash, no trailing slash, and both halves matter:
#   - no trailing slash, because post-split these may be symlinks into the data root,
#     and a trailing slash matches only a real directory
#   - leading slash to anchor at the repo root, because an unanchored `jobs` matches
#     EVERY path component of that name — which silently excluded example-data/jobs/,
#     the whole point of the example dataset, from the repo
/jobs
/exports
/site
# Personal archive: career-coach materials, third-party PDFs. Lives in the data
# root, never in the toolkit (plan §1 blocker 6).
/extras
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-wal
db.sqlite3-shm
db.sqlite3-journal
.jobstudio-data
# Generated by `init` and full of absolute paths — personal to one machine (§5.4).
jobstudio.code-workspace

# NOT ignored: backups/django/dump.json — the frozen test fixture FIXTURE_DIRS
# reads (tests.py pins the name). The user's own dumps are timestamped and live
# in <data-root>/backups/django/. Two different needs, two different paths.

# django (see log/2026-09-07-django-frontend-plan.md)
src/web/local_settings.py
collectstatic/
tools/db-bootstrap
build/

# Personal denylist for tools/make-public-tree — see .private-terms.example
.private-terms

# Allowed-anyway list for the derived tracked-company check in tools/make-public-tree —
# see .tracked-company-exceptions.example. Ignored for the same reason .private-terms is:
# the set of companies you track is itself the disclosure.
.tracked-company-exceptions
